<title>UK: UK PIA's compliance chief resigns.</title>
<headline>UK PIA's compliance chief resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of compliance at Britain's Personal Investment Authority, which regulates the UK pension industry, resigned last week, according to UK press reports.</p>
<p>The Financial Times quoted a PIA spokeswoman saying David Cranston left the PIA on Friday to pursue other business interests.</p>
<p>The regulator denied industry suggestions that Cranston was dismissed as part of an effort to soothe the new Labour government's anger over the PIA's handling of Britain's pensions mis-selling scandal, said the Financial Times.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
